## 🚀 Installation and Setup

Follow these steps to run the project locally.

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/ujwala42/Ecommerce-Logistics-Performance-Analysis.git
```

### 2. Navigate to the Project Folder

```bash
cd Ecommerce-Logistics-Performance-Analysis
```

### 3. Create a Virtual Environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

### 4. Activate the Virtual Environment

**Windows PowerShell:**

```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

If PowerShell blocks activation, run:

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
```

Then activate the environment again.

**Windows Command Prompt (CMD):**

```cmd
venv\Scripts\activate.bat
```

### 5. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 6. Run the Jupyter Notebook

Open the following file in VS Code:

```text
notebooks/logistics_analysis.ipynb
```

Execute the notebook cells to perform data cleaning, analysis, and visualization.

### 7. Run the Streamlit Dashboard

```bash
python -m streamlit run app.py
```

The dashboard will open in your web browser.

Local URL:

```text
http://localhost:8501
```

